  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Heather Choate organises the annual customer trip and customer meeting. A round starts with a trip proposal or invitation sent to the business, then asks each desk to name the customers and employees it designates, sets deadlines for replacing guests who cannot attend, and finishes with a final guest list, activities and a rooming list sent for review. Reminders go out as the trip approaches.",
    "steps": [
      "The organiser circulates the trip proposal for approval.",
      "The invitation to the customer meeting is sent out.",
      "Desks are asked to forward their customer and employee trip designations.",
      "Replacements for declined guests are collected by a stated deadline.",
      "The final guest list with activities and the rooming list are sent for review.",
      "A reminder goes out as the trip approaches."
    ],
    "approach": "A shared guest tracker holding designations, RSVPs, replacements, activities and room assignments, from which the final guest and rooming lists are produced directly, with a standard request message to desks carrying the cut-off date.",
    "rationale": "Each round rebuilds the same lists from desk replies; one spreadsheet layout for designations, RSVPs and rooming removes the retyping and makes the final lists a by-product rather than a separate job.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
